 "claim": "The four-place knots are exactly the relations whose excluded states form a non-empty independent set of the 4-cube (a three-place projection is full iff no two excluded states differ in one place): 742 relations in 20 classes under flips and permutations, 4 value-free (FOUR-PLACE A) and 16 preferring a value. Only parity is Schaefer-tractable. Only the clause (one excluded state) has a forcing value at every place; it never fails on 4-regular 4-uniform systems, because a perfect matching of lines to points (Hall) lets each line's matched point take a forcing value (Tovey's argument).",
